{# ============================================================================
   HYPER · مجموعة مميزة — merchandising row
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
     New Arrivals                                    New Arrivals   Hot Items
     One line of supporting copy.                    ‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾
     ┌──────────┐ ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐
     │ promo    │ │ card   │ │ card   │ │ card   │ │ card  ⋯
     └──────────┘ └────────┘ └────────┘ └────────┘ └────────┘
     ▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬────────────────────────────────      ( ‹ ) ( › )

   ── Tabs ──
   Three fixed slots (`tab1_*` … `tab3_*`), NOT repeatable blocks.

   ⚠️  They were blocks, each holding its own `products` picker, and the Theme
   Editor would not render the block's settings at all with one there. No
   original widget in this theme puts `products` inside a `blocks` entry —
   `media` and `menu` are the only pickers that appear in one — so the type is
   supported at widget level only. Three slots is also what the design asks for;
   the reference has two. Do not move these back into blocks.

   A slot with no LABEL is not a tab and renders nothing. With fewer than two
   labelled slots no tab strip renders at all — the section is just a row. Every set is rendered
   SERVER-SIDE and toggled with x-show, not fetched on click: the sets are
   already in the page JSON, so a fetch would be a round-trip to redisplay data
   the browser is holding. Each set gets its OWN Swiper, built lazily the first
   time its tab is opened — a Swiper initialised inside `display: none` measures
   every slide as zero and lays the row out on top of itself.

   ── RTL ──
   ⚠️  Swiper has NO `rtl` init option. It resolves direction off the ELEMENT —
   `el.dir` first, then the computed `direction` — so the only reliable way to
   set it is the `dir` attribute written on the .swiper below. Passing `rtl:` in
   the config is silently ignored. Inherited computed style would usually be
   enough here (the <html> is rtl), but the attribute also survives the Theme
   Editor re-injecting this section outside the document's direction context.
   Once it is set, prev/next stay semantic and Swiper maps them to the correct
   visual side; `.rtl-flip` mirrors the chevron glyph to match. The scrollbar
   fill follows the same flag, so the rail fills from the correct edge.

   ── Cards ──
   Rendered by ui/product-card.njk on the server and by HayatCard.build() when
   they arrive over AJAX. Both live in one place each; this widget never writes
   card markup itself. `variant: catalog` is the one used here — see 15.9.1.

   ── Empty states ──
   A merchant drops this section in before picking anything, so an empty tab
   falls back to fetching the newest products. And if the STORE itself is empty,
   the row draws placeholder cards rather than a bare apology: the merchant sees
   the real layout at the real size, waiting to be filled.

   All styling lives in assets/style.css → "15.7 PRODUCT CARD", "15.9.1 CATALOG
   VARIANT" and "15.8 PRODUCT ROW".
   ========================================================================= #}

{% set id = widget.id %}
{% set d = widget.data %}
{# Fixed slots, listed once here so the three loops below stay in step. `key`
   is the pane's id suffix and doubles as its Alpine index. #}
{% set tabs = [
  { label: d.tab1_label | default('', true), products: d.tab1_products | default([]) },
  { label: d.tab2_label | default('', true), products: d.tab2_products | default([]) },
  { label: d.tab3_label | default('', true), products: d.tab3_products | default([]) }
] %}
{# Counted with an inline-if sum rather than a loop: Nunjucks scopes `{% set %}`
   to the block it runs in, so a counter incremented inside `{% for %}` reads
   back as its pre-loop value outside it. #}
{% set labelled = (1 if d.tab1_label else 0) + (1 if d.tab2_label else 0) + (1 if d.tab3_label else 0) %}
{# On a product page the first empty slot takes the platform's related products,
   and no slot ever shows the product being looked at. A pushed array for each
   slot, because `{% set %}` inside a loop does not survive it. #}
{% set openId = context.product._id if context.product else '' %}
{% set relatedCtx = context.related_products or [] %}
{% set paneLists = [] %}
{% for tb in tabs %}
  {% set src = tb.products if (tb.products | length) > 0 else (relatedCtx if (loop.first and openId) else []) %}
  {% set kept = [] %}
  {% for rp in src %}{% if not openId or rp._id != openId %}{% set _ = kept.push(rp) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
  {% set _ = paneLists.push(kept) %}
{% endfor %}
{% set tabCount = labelled %}

{% set title = d.title | default(t('defaults.new_arrivals'), true) %}
{% set subtitle = d.subtitle | default('', true) %}
{# ---- Fallback size ----
   Was a Theme Editor control; fixed at the value the carousel was sized
   for. It only ever applied to the automatic "newest products" fallback —
   a hand-picked list is shown in full — and it is still both SENT to the
   API and applied with `slice` further down; see the note there. #}
{% set limit = 12 %}
{% set colsD = d.columns_desktop | default('4', true) %}
{% set colsM = d.columns_mobile | default('2', true) %}
{% set ratio = d.card_image_ratio | default('1x1') %}
{% set bg = d.background | default('white') %}
{% set showArrows = d.show_arrows | default(true) %}
{% set showProgress = d.show_progress | default(true) %}
{% set viewAllText = d.view_all_text | default(t('common.view_all'), true) %}
{% set viewAllUrl = d.view_all_url | default('/shop') %}

{% set promoOn = d.promo_enabled | default(false) %}
{% set promoImg = d.promo_image.fileUrl if d.promo_image and d.promo_image.fileUrl else (d.promo_image if d.promo_image is string else '') %}
{# no photo yet → bundled demo photo (CC0, docs/demo-images.md) #}
{% if not promoImg %}{% set promoImg = 'demo-promo.jpg' | assets %}{% endif %}
{% set promoUrl = d.promo_url | default('/shop') %}

{# The fractional part is the point: a card cut by the viewport edge is what
   tells a shopper the row scrolls. A whole number reads as a finished grid.
   The sliver is also the width dial — every extra 0.1 of a card shown at the
   edge comes straight out of the cards themselves. #}
{% set perView = colsD | float + 0.4 %}
{% set perViewMd = 3.4 if colsD | float > 3 else 2.4 %}
{% set perViewSm = colsM | float + 0.25 %}

{% set isRtl = (localization.language | default('ar')) != 'en' %}


{# The root background is INLINE, so it beats every stylesheet rule — which is
   why it reads `var(--hy-sec-bg, …)`. The section-colours picker overrides the
   custom property, not the declaration. Do not collapse it back. #}
<section id="hy-cp-{{ id }}"
         class="hy-prow"
         style="background: var(--hy-sec-bg, {{ 'var(--color-bg-tertiary)' if bg == 'well' else 'var(--color-surface)' }});
                padding-block: var(--section-py);"
         x-data="{ tab: 0 }"
         {# If slot 1 is unlabelled but slot 2 is, no button carries index 0 and
            `tab: 0` would open a pane nothing can switch away from. Read the
            rendered buttons rather than computing an index in the template. #}
         x-init="if (!$el.querySelector('.hy-prow-tab[data-i=\'' + tab + '\']')) {
                   const first = $el.querySelector('.hy-prow-tab');
                   if (first) tab = Number(first.dataset.i);
                 }">
  <div class="hy-container">

    {# ═══════════════════ head ═══════════════════ #}
    {% if title or subtitle or labelled > 1 or viewAllText %}
      <div class="hy-prow-head">
        <div class="hy-prow-headings">
          {% if title %}<h2 class="hy-prow-title">{{ title }}</h2>{% endif %}
          {% if subtitle %}<p class="hy-prow-sub">{{ subtitle }}</p>{% endif %}
        </div>

        {# The tab strip and the "view all" link share the head's end edge, so
           only one of them can have it. Tabs win when there are any: they change
           what the row SHOWS, while the link only leaves it. #}
        {% if labelled < 2 and viewAllText %}
          <a href="{{ viewAllUrl }}" class="hy-cgrid-all">
            <span>{{ viewAllText }}</span>
            <svg class="rtl-flip" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                 stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m9 6 6 6-6 6"/>
            </svg>
          </a>
        {% endif %}

        {% if labelled > 1 %}
          <div class="hy-prow-tabs" role="tablist">
            {# Unlabelled slots are skipped. `loop.index0` still counts them, so
               the indices stay in step with the panels below. There is no
               fallback label on purpose — a shared one makes every unnamed tab
               read identically. #}
            {% for tb in tabs %}
              {% if tb.label %}
                <button type="button"
                        role="tab"
                        data-i="{{ loop.index0 }}"
                        class="hy-prow-tab"
                        :class="tab === {{ loop.index0 }} && 'is-active'"
                        :aria-selected="tab === {{ loop.index0 }} ? 'true' : 'false'"
                        @click="tab = {{ loop.index0 }}; $dispatch('hy-tab-shown', { id: {{ loop.index0 }} })">
                  {{ tb.label }}
                </button>
              {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
          </div>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    {% endif %}

    {# ═══════════════════ panels ═══════════════════ #}
    {# A slot renders a pane when it is labelled, and slot 1 renders even
       unlabelled so a section with no tabs at all is still a product row. #}
    {% for tb in tabs %}
      {% set products = paneLists[loop.index0] %}
      {% set hasServer = (products | length) > 0 %}
      {% set pane = id ~ '-' ~ loop.index0 %}
      {% if tb.label or (loop.first and labelled == 0) %}

      {# x-show, not x-if: the inactive panel stays in the DOM so its Swiper can
         be built on first reveal and its images can start loading. #}
      <div class="hy-prow-panel"
           id="hy-cpPanel-{{ pane }}"
           data-pane="{{ loop.index0 }}"
           role="tabpanel"
           {% if labelled > 1 %}x-show="tab === {{ loop.index0 }}"{% endif %}>

        {# `--pr-cols*` must match `slidesPerView` in the script: the CSS sizes the
           slides too, so the row is correct on the first frame instead of
           flashing one full-width card while Swiper boots. #}
        <div class="hy-prow-stage"
             style="--pr-cols: {{ perViewSm }};
                    --pr-cols-md: {{ perViewMd }};
                    --pr-cols-lg: {{ perView }};">
          {# `dir` is load-bearing — see the RTL note at the top of this file. #}
          <div id="hy-cpSw-{{ pane }}" class="swiper" dir="{{ 'rtl' if isRtl else 'ltr' }}">
            <div id="hy-cpWrapper-{{ pane }}" class="swiper-wrapper">

              {% if promoOn and loop.first %}
                {# The promo tile rides in the FIRST slide rather than sitting
                   outside the slider: outside it would need its own column and
                   the row's scroll would start past it, which on a phone hides
                   it entirely behind the first product. #}
                <div class="swiper-slide">
                  <a href="{{ promoUrl }}" class="hy-promo">
                    {% if promoImg %}
                      <img src="{{ promoImg }}" alt="{{ d.promo_title | default('', true) }}" loading="lazy" class="hy-promo-img"/>
                    {% endif %}
                    <span class="hy-promo-scrim"></span>
                    <span class="hy-promo-body">
                      {% if d.promo_eyebrow %}<span class="hy-promo-eyebrow">{{ d.promo_eyebrow }}</span>{% endif %}
                      {% if d.promo_title %}<span class="hy-promo-title">{{ d.promo_title }}</span>{% endif %}
                    </span>
                    {% if d.promo_cta_text %}
                      <span class="hy-promo-cta">{{ d.promo_cta_text }}</span>
                    {% endif %}
                  </a>
                </div>
              {% endif %}

              {% for p in products %}
                <div class="swiper-slide">
                  {% ui "product-card.njk", product=p, image_ratio=ratio, variant='catalog' %}
                </div>
              {% endfor %}

              {% if not hasServer %}
                {# Placeholders for a store with nothing in it yet. They live
                   INSIDE the wrapper so the row has its true height from the
                   first paint; the script replaces them the moment real
                   products arrive, and leaves them standing if none ever do. #}
                {% ui "placeholder.njk", kind='product', count=colsD, image_ratio=ratio, variant='catalog', wrap='swiper-slide' %}
              {% endif %}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        {# ---- controls: rail on the start edge, arrows on the end edge ----
           One row so the two can never drift apart vertically, and so the rail
           gets whatever width the arrows leave it at every breakpoint. #}
        {% if showArrows or showProgress %}
          <div class="hy-prow-controls" id="hy-cpCtl-{{ pane }}" {% if not hasServer %}style="display: none;"{% endif %}>
            {% if showProgress %}
              <div id="hy-cpProg-{{ pane }}" class="hy-prow-rail"></div>
            {% endif %}
            {% if showArrows %}
              <div class="hy-prow-nav">
                <button type="button" id="hy-cpPrev-{{ pane }}" class="hy-prow-arrow" aria-label="{{ t('common.prev') }}">
                  <svg class="rtl-flip" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" aria-hidden="true">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 6 9 12l6 6"/>
                  </svg>
                </button>
                <button type="button" id="hy-cpNext-{{ pane }}" class="hy-prow-arrow" aria-label="{{ t('common.next') }}">
                  <svg class="rtl-flip" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" aria-hidden="true">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m9 6 6 6-6 6"/>
                  </svg>
                </button>
              </div>
            {% endif %}
          </div>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}

  </div>
</section>

<script>
  /* Runs once main.js has defined Qumra / HayatCard. This script sits inside the
     page body and main.js loads at its end, so running immediately threw
     "Qumra is not defined" and the row never filled (the newest-products
     fallback and the empty-store demo both lived behind it). */
  (function (run) {
    if (window.Qumra && window.HayatCard) run();
    else document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', run);
  })(function () {
    var SECTION = document.getElementById('hy-cp-{{ id }}');
    if (!SECTION) return;

    var LIMIT = {{ limit | int }};
    var OPEN_ID = {{ openId | dump | safe }};

    /* Mirrors the locals passed to ui "product-card.njk" above, so an AJAX card
       and a server card resolve their options identically. An empty ratio means
       "inherit the theme setting", which HayatCard already does through its own
       defaults — so it must not be sent as an empty string. */
    var cardOpts = { variant: 'catalog' };
    {% if ratio %}cardOpts.imageRatio = '{{ ratio }}';{% endif %}

    /* Only the slots that actually rendered a pane. */
    var panes = [
      {% for tb in tabs %}{% if tb.label or (loop.first and labelled == 0) %}
      {
        key: '{{ id }}-{{ loop.index0 }}',
        hasServer: {{ 'true' if (paneLists[loop.index0] | length) > 0 else 'false' }},
        sw: null
      },
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    ];

    function build(pane) {
      /* Already built, or the panel is hidden — a Swiper initialised inside
         `display: none` measures every slide as zero width and stacks the whole
         row on top of itself, with no error anywhere. */
      if (pane.sw) return;
      var el = document.getElementById('hy-cpSw-' + pane.key);
      if (!el || !el.offsetParent || typeof Swiper === 'undefined') return;

      pane.sw = new Swiper(el, {
        /* Direction comes from the element's `dir` attribute, NOT from here —
           see the RTL note at the top of this file. */
        direction: 'horizontal',
        slidesPerView: {{ perViewSm | float }},
        spaceBetween: 16,
        watchOverflow: true,
        breakpoints: {
          768:  { slidesPerView: {{ perViewMd | float }}, spaceBetween: 20 },
          1024: { slidesPerView: {{ perView | float }},   spaceBetween: 24 }
        },
        {% if showArrows %}
        navigation: { prevEl: '#hy-cpPrev-' + pane.key, nextEl: '#hy-cpNext-' + pane.key },
        {% endif %}
        {% if showProgress %}
        scrollbar: { el: '#hy-cpProg-' + pane.key, draggable: true, hide: false },
        {% endif %}
        a11y: { enabled: true }
      });
    }

    /* First pane is visible on load; the rest are built when their tab opens. */
    panes.forEach(function (p, i) { if (i === 0) build(p); });

    SECTION.addEventListener('hy-tab-shown', function (e) {
      /* The event carries the SLOT index, which is not the array position once
         an unlabelled slot has been skipped — look the pane up by its key. */
      var want = '{{ id }}-' + (e.detail && e.detail.id);
      var pane = null;
      panes.forEach(function (p) { if (p.key === want) pane = p; });
      if (!pane) return;
      /* One frame later: x-show has to have cleared `display: none` before
         Swiper can measure anything. */
      requestAnimationFrame(function () {
        build(pane);
        if (pane.sw) pane.sw.update();
      });
    });

    /* ---- Empty tabs fall back to the newest products ---- */
    panes.forEach(function (pane) {
      if (pane.hasServer) return;

      /* LIMIT is sent AND applied, and both halves are load-bearing.

         /ajax/search/products documents only q, minPrice, maxPrice,
         collectionId, minRating and sort — no page size at all. So this used to
         ask for nothing and trim the answer, which made the setting work in one
         direction only: below the endpoint's own page size it cut the list, and
         above it nothing happened, because there was no second request to fetch
         more with. That is what "the control does nothing" looked like.

         The docs are known to be incomplete — see the note beside the price
         bounds in main.js `_applyFilters`, where the same reasoning sends two
         spellings of the same filter. Both spellings of a page size go out
         here for the same reason: an endpoint that understands either now
         returns the right number, and one that understands neither ignores two
         unknown query params exactly as it ignored none.

         `slice` stays regardless. It is the only guarantee that a server which
         ignores both does not paint 60 cards into a carousel sized for 12. */
      Qumra.search.search('', {
        sort: 'created-desc',
        limit: LIMIT,
        'resources[limit]': LIMIT
      }).then(function (data) {
        var list = (data && (data.products || data.data || data.results)) || [];
        /* The newest list can hold the product being looked at. */
        if (OPEN_ID) list = list.filter(function (p) { return p && p._id !== OPEN_ID; });
        /* Nothing came back — the store itself is empty. Show the demo catalogue
           (main.js HayatDemo: real photos, inert cards) so a fresh install is
           never a row of grey boxes. Any store with one product never sees it. */
        var inEditor = document.documentElement.classList.contains('hy-editor');
        if (!list.length && Qumra.demo && inEditor) list = Qumra.demo.products(LIMIT);

        var wrapper = document.getElementById('hy-cpWrapper-' + pane.key);
        if (!wrapper) return;
        /* Demo cards are for the merchant in the editor only. A shopper on an
           empty store gets no section at all rather than fake products. */
        if (!list.length) {
          if (!inEditor && wrapper.closest('section')) wrapper.closest('section').setAttribute('data-hy-empty', '');
          return;                               /* editor: leave the placeholders standing */
        }

        wrapper.innerHTML = list.slice(0, LIMIT).map(function (p) {
          return '<div class="swiper-slide">' + HayatCard.build(p, cardOpts) + '</div>';
        }).join('');

        if (window.Alpine) {
          wrapper.querySelectorAll('[x-data]').forEach(function (el) { Alpine.initTree(el); });
        }

        var ctl = document.getElementById('hy-cpCtl-' + pane.key);
        if (ctl) ctl.style.display = '';

        pane.hasServer = true;
        if (pane.sw) { pane.sw.update(); } else { build(pane); }
      }).catch(function () { /* placeholders stay */ });
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  #hy-cp-{{ id }} .hy-pcard--catalog .hy-pcard-frame {
    {# was a Theme Editor control; fixed at the drawn value — see the note
       in any sibling widget's radius block. #}
    --hy-cat-radius: 10px;
  }
</style>

{# Per-section palette. Emits nothing unless `colors_enabled` is on, so the
   switch IS the revert. Must stay after the widget's own <style>. #}
{% ui "section-colors.njk", scope='#hy-cp-' ~ id, c=d %}
